Let $A = \begin{pmatrix} . \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ , \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{pmatrix}$. We want to find $\det(A)$.
We have
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= \sec^2 x \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} - 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} + 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) + (\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sec^2 x \cos^2 x (\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} \cos^2 x (\frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x}) - \cos^2 x \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \left(\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x\right) - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^6 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x - \cos^6 x + \cos^4 x \sin^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x (1 - \cos^4 x + \cos^2 x \sin^2 x)}{\sin^2 x} - \cos^2 x \end{align*}
Alternatively,
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - 1(\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) + 1(\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} (\cos^2 x \cdot \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} \cos^2 x) - \frac{\cos^2 x \cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} (\frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x}) - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x \cos^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x (\cos^2 x - 1)}{\sin^2 x \cos^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x - 1}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x - 1}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x - 1}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1 - \cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x - 1 + 1 - \cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x - \cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x(1 - \cos^2 x)}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x \sin^2 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cos^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x = \cos^4 x \end{align*} 
Therefore, $\det(A) = \cos^4 x$.

\boxed{\cos^4 x}

