\begin{enumerate}
    \item Define the sample space.
    \item Calculate the probability of a single outcome condition.
    \item Calculate the probability of the desired event.
\end{enumerate}

\begin{enumerate}
    \item The sample space is $6^6 = 46656$.
    \item The probability of rolling a 1 is $\frac{1}{6}$, and the probability of rolling a 2 is $\frac{1}{6}$.
    \item We need to choose 2 dice out of 6 to show a 1, and the remaining 4 dice must show a 2.
    The number of ways to choose 2 dice to show a 1 is $\binom{6}{2} = \frac{6!}{2!4!} = \frac{6 \times 5}{2 \times 1} = 15$.
    The number of ways to choose 4 dice to show a 2 is $\binom{4}{4} = 1$.
    So the number of favorable outcomes is $\binom{6}{2} \times \binom{4}{4} = 15 \times 1 = 15$.
    The probability of the desired event is $\frac{15}{6^6} = \frac{15}{46656} = \frac{5}{15552}$.
\end{enumerate}

\boxed{\frac{5}{15552}}

