Calculating this product:
$20 \cdot 19 = 380$
$380 \cdot 18 = 380 \cdot (10 + 8) = 3800 + 3040 = 6840$

Therefore, there are 6840 ways to select a president, a vice-president, and a treasurer from the 20 members of the math club, where no member can hold more than one office.

