\begin{center}
\textbf{Problem:} If $|z| = 5$, what is $|\overline{z}^2|$?
\end{center}
We are given that $|z| = 5$. We know that the magnitude of the conjugate of a complex number $z$, denoted by $\overline{z}$, is the same as the magnitude of the complex number $z$. In other words, $|\overline{z}| = |z|$. 

We want to find $|\overline{z}^2|$. We know that $|z^2| = |z|^2$. So, $|\overline{z}^2| = |(\overline{z})^2| = |\overline{z}|^2$. 
Since $|\overline{z}| = |z|$, we have $|\overline{z}^2| = |z|^2$. 

Given $|z| = 5$, we have $|\overline{z}^2| = |z|^2 = 5^2 = 25$. 

Therefore, $|\overline{z}^2| = 25$.

\boxed{25}
\boxed{25}

