The answer should be expressed as a decimal value.

First find the time in seconds it takes to paint all the dimples. The shop class takes $2$ seconds to paint one dimple and there are $300$ dimples. So the total time in seconds is $2 \times 300 = 600$ seconds.
Now, we convert the time from seconds to minutes. Since there are $60$ seconds in a minute, we divide the total time in seconds by $60$ to get the time in minutes. 
So, the time in minutes is $\frac{600}{60} = 10$ minutes.

