\begin{align*} \frac{2}{5}E + E &= 35 \\ \frac{2E + 5E}{5} &= 35 \\ \frac{7E}{5} &= 35 \\ 7E &= 35 \cdot 5 \\ 7E &= 175 \\ E &= \frac{175}{7} \\ E &= 25\end{align*} 
Now we can find $L$:
$$L = \frac{2}{5}E = \frac{2}{5}(25) = 2 \cdot 5 = 10$$ 
The difference between Lenny's and Larry's amount is:
$$E - L = 25 - 10 = 15$$ 
Lenny has $15 more than Larry.

