How many functions are both even and odd? (Assume , that the domain of the function is the set ? of all real numbers.)
\end{center}
Let $f(x)$ be a function that is both even and odd.
If $f(x)$ is even, then $f(-x) = f(x)$ for all $x$ in the domain.
If $f(x)$ is odd, then $f(-x) = -f(x)$ for all $x$ in the domain.
If $f(x)$ is both even and odd, then we must have $f(-x) = f(x) = -f(x)$.
Thus, $f(x) = -f(x)$, which implies $2f(x) = 0$, so $f(x) = 0$ for all $x$.
Therefore, the only function that is both even and odd is the function $f(x) = 0$.
The number of such functions is 1.
