We want the smallest positive angle $\theta,$ so we take $k = -1.$ Then $\theta = -\frac{45^\circ}{2} - 90^\circ (-1) = -\frac{45^\circ}{2} + 90^\circ = \frac{-45^\circ + 180^\circ}{2} = \frac{135^\circ}{2} = 67.5^\circ.$

Comparing $9^\circ$ and $67.5^\circ,$ we have $\theta = 9^\circ.$

We can also use the identity $\sin x = \cos (90^\circ - x).$
